'</ul>',
'</div>'))
,p_list_template_current=>'<li class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-item amc-TBentoLaunchpad-item--#A01# is-current"><a class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-link" href="#LINK#" aria-current="page"><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-glyph fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-chip"><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-icon fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-body"><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-title">#TEXT#</span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-desc">#A02#</span></span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-metric">#A03#</span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-go fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></li>'
,p_list_template_noncurrent=>'<li class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-item amc-TBentoLaunchpad-item--#A01#"><a class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-link" href="#LINK#"><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-glyph fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-chip"><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-icon fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-body"><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-title">#TEXT#</span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-desc">#A02#</span></span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-metric">#A03#</span><span class="amc-TBentoLaunchpad-go fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></li>'
,p_list_template_name=>'AMC Bento Launchpad'
,p_internal_name=>'AMC_TPL_BENTO_LAUNCHPAD'
,p_theme_id=>42
,p_css_file_urls=>'#APP_FILES#amc-templates/amc-tpl-bento-launchpad.css'
,p_a01_label=>'Tile size'
,p_a02_label=>'Description'
,p_a03_label=>'Metric'
,p_list_template_comment=>'List template for a List region. User Defined Attribute 1 sets the tile size: wide (two columns), tall (two rows) or large (two by two, filled with the primary color); leave it empty for a normal tile, and other values are ignored. Attribute 2 is a short description and Attribute 3 a metric such as ''128'' or ''SAR 4.2M'' (use an application item substitution to keep it live). The grid uses 1 column below 480px of region width (tiles become rows), 2 columns up to 760px, 4 up to 1180px and 6 beyond; tall, wide and large tiles switch their inner layout to show a big metric. While one tile has the pointer the others step back. Everything works with the keyboard in list order, with a visible focus ring. Template options: Tinted tiles, Compact rows, Mono large tile, Hide big icons.'
);
end;
